<title>UK: Russia's oil port Novorossiisk closed by bad weath.</title>
<headline>Russia's oil port Novorossiisk closed by bad weath.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian Black Sea oil outlet Novorossiisk was closed on Monday by bad weather, a reliable shipping source said.</p>
<p>The terminal closed on Sunday evening with winds blowing at force 8-9 on the Beaufort scale.</p>
<p>Russia's Baltic outlet at Ventspils in Latvia reopened on Monday morning after closing overnight on Sunday because of highs winds.</p>
<p>Pipeline deliveries to Ventspils were closed at 0300 local time when storage tanks reached capacity.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 17 542 8060</p>
</text>
